    "teacher_markdown": "### **Teacher Tips**\r\n\r\n**Students may focus on the password instead of the loop**\r\n\r\nSome students will inspect the generated password characters rather than the loop that creates them. Encourage them to compare the expected and actual lengths by asking: **\"How many times does the loop actually run?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nfor (let i = 0; i < length - 1; i++) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nHelp students connect the number of loop iterations to the number of characters generated.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n **Students may overlook the loop condition**\r\n\r\nStudents often check the starting value (`i = 0`) and increment (`i++`) but skip examining the condition. Point them to the Loop Debugging Checklist by asking: **\"Which part of the loop decides when it stops?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\ni < length - 1\r\n```\r\n\r\nCorrected version:\r\n```javascript\r\ni < length\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces that a small change in the condition can change how many times the loop runs.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n**Students may test only one input value**\r\n\r\nStudents may fix the loop after testing a single length and assume the bug is solved. Encourage them to test several values by asking: **\"Does the expected length match the actual length for 1, 5, and 10 characters?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant output:\r\n```javascript\r\nlengthMessage.textContent =\r\n  \"Expected length: \" + length +\r\n  \" | Actual length: \" + password.length;\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis helps students develop the habit of verifying fixes with multiple test cases.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n **Students may change the wrong part of the loop**\r\n\r\nSome students may modify `i++` or the starting value instead of the stopping condition. Encourage them to isolate the bug by asking: **\"Which part of the loop is causing it to stop one iteration too early?\"**\r\n\r\nRelevant code:\r\n```javascript\r\nfor (let i = 0; i < length - 1; i++) {\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis reinforces the three parts of a `for` loop:\r\n- Initialization\r\n- Condition\r\n- Update"
  },
